Aim
To write a Python program to demonstrate various list operations and built-in functions, such as append, insert, remove, pop, count, index, sort, reverse, copy, extend, maximum, minimum, sum, and clear.

Algorithm
1.Start the program.
2.Create a list number containing the elements [10, 20, 30, 40, 50].
3.Display the original list.
4.Find and display the length of the list using len().
5.Add 60 to the end of the list using append().
6.Insert 25 at index 2 using insert().
7.Remove 25 from the list using remove().
8.Remove the last element using pop().
9.Count the occurrences of 20 using count() and display the result.
Find the index of 30 using index() and display the result.
Sort the list in ascending order using sort().
Reverse the list using reverse().
Create a copy of the list using copy() and display it.
Add 70 and 80 to the list using extend().
Find and display the maximum value using max().
Find and display the minimum value using min().
Find and display the sum of all elements using sum().
Remove all elements from the list using clear().
Display the cleared list.
Stop the program.


CODE
number = [10,20,30,40,50]
print("original list:",number)

print("length:",len(number))

number.append(60)
print("After append:",number)

number.insert(2,25)
print("After insert:",number)

number.remove(25)
print("after remove:",number)

number.pop()
print("after pop:",number)

print("count of 20:",
      number.count(20))

print("index of 30:",
      number.index(30))

number.sort()
print("after sort:",number)

number.reverse()
print("after reverse:",number)

new_list = number.copy()
print("copied list:",new_list)

number.extend([70,80])
print("after extend:",number)

print("maximum:",max(number))

print("minimum:",min(number))

print("sum:",sum(number))

number.clear()
print("after clear:",number)
      


